@startuml sequence-ota-agent
' Sequence: one firmware update, from OtaAgent::start() to onDone, with the
' three threads that take part marked. REQ-INTEGRATION-016, ADR-0035.
'
' Grounded in real source:
'   - src/integration/OtaAgent.h/.cpp   (start, frameSink, progress, Impl)
'   - src/integration/OtaSession.h/.cpp (start / onFrame / onTick, ADR-0034)
'   - src/integration/SerialBackend.h   (send + FrameSink, ADR-0032/0033)
'   - src/integration/FlashFrameParser.h (bytes -> frames, on the backend thread)
'   - docs/protocols/uart-flash-v1.md   (section 5, the order of the messages)

title OTA update - OtaAgent owns the session, the clock and the link

skinparam shadowing false

actor "Caller\n(bootstrap / UI)" as Caller

box "caller's thread" #LightGray
  participant "OtaAgent\n(thin forwarders)" as Agent
end box

box "agent thread (jthread + io_context)" #LightYellow
  participant "OtaAgent::Impl\nbeginUpdate / onTick / onFrame" as Impl
  participant "OtaSession\n(Boost.SML table)" as Session
end box

box "transport thread (SerialBackend's io_context)" #LightBlue
  participant "SerialBackend\n::send / routeChunk" as Backend
  participant "FlashFrameParser" as Parser
end box

participant "Board\n(Nucleo bootloader)" as Board

== wiring, before anything runs ==
Caller -> Agent : OtaAgent(send, image, version, timing, onDone)
Caller -> Agent : frameSink()
Agent --> Caller : std::function holding a **weak_ptr<Impl>**
Caller -> Backend : SerialBackend(device, baud, readingSink, **that sink**)

== start ==
Caller -> Agent : start()
Agent -> Impl : post(beginUpdate) then launch the jthread
note over Agent: returns at once; the caller\nnever drives the session
Impl -> Session : start(now)
Session --> Impl : INFO_REQ bytes
Impl -> Backend : send(bytes)   (the injected SendFn)
Backend -> Board : bytes over UART
Impl -> Impl : publishProgress()  (under progressMutex)
Impl -> Impl : scheduleTick()  (steady_timer, weak_ptr handler)

== each answer ==
Board -> Backend : reply bytes
Backend -> Parser : consume(bytes)
Parser --> Backend : FlashFrame (0xA5, read by LEN, CRC ok)
Backend -> Agent : frameSink(frame)
note right of Agent
  Runs on the transport thread.
  lock() the weak_ptr: expired means
  the agent is gone, drop the frame.
end note
Agent -> Impl : post(onFrame(frame))  (crosses to the agent thread)
Impl -> Session : onFrame(frame, now)
Session --> Impl : the next frame's bytes, or nothing
Impl -> Backend : send(bytes)
Impl -> Impl : publishProgress()

== the clock ==
loop every 5 ms while the update runs
  Impl -> Session : onTick(now)
  Session --> Impl : a resend if an answer is late,\nor the next step if a wait elapsed
  opt something to send
    Impl -> Backend : send(bytes)
  end
  Impl -> Impl : publishProgress() ; scheduleTick()
end

== a link that died ==
Impl -> Backend : send(bytes)
Backend --> Impl : **false** (not running)
Impl -> Impl : transportFailed = true, published at once
note over Impl
  Reported beside the session, never into it:
  ADR-0034 kept OtaSession I/O-free. The session
  keeps ticking its own resend budget out and
  reaches its own terminal state on its own.
end note

== the end ==
Session --> Impl : stage() == Done (or Failed)
Impl -> Impl : fireDoneIfTerminal()  (once, ever)
Impl -> Caller : onDone(progress)   ' on the agent thread
note over Impl: the tick is not re-armed,\nso the io_context drains

== reading it from anywhere ==
Caller -> Agent : progress()
Agent --> Caller : a copy of OtaProgress,\ntaken under progressMutex

== shutdown ==
Caller -> Agent : stop()  /  ~OtaAgent()
Agent -> Impl : context.stop() then join  (idempotent, noexcept)

note across
  Three threads, one rule: OtaSession is touched only on the agent thread.
  The frame sink does nothing but lock a weak_ptr and post across, so a frame
  that arrives after the agent is destroyed is dropped, not delivered to freed
  state. progress() is a copy under a mutex, so a UI never reaches the session.
end note

@enduml
